#==============================================================================================
#
#   run_test262 - The ECMA test262 runner for luce-js
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of QuickJS's run-test262.c (QuickJS 2026-06-04): runs test262 with the same
#       configuration files (test262.conf), the same harness semantics (includes, the
#       flags onlyStrict/noStrict/raw/module/async/CanBlockIsFalse, negative tests, the
#       $262 host object with its agents and realms), the same known-errors file
#       comparison (test262_errors.txt, updated with -u) and the same progress output.
#       Tests run on worker threads, one JSRuntime per test, as upstream does. This
#       fragment holds the imports, the C library bindings, the global state and the
#       string and name-list helpers; the others follow run-test262.c in order.
#
#       Differences from the C: the agent and report lists are singly linked lists with
#       a tail instead of list_head; the progress thread polls every 50 ms instead of a
#       timed condition wait; print_error takes a formatted line (Base functions are not
#       variadic); threads get 8 MB stacks instead of 2 MB (compiler-issues/
#       frame-slots-not-shared). Everything else, including every option, is ported.
#
#       Build: luce-base build tests/run_test262 -o build/run-test262 --release
#       Run from tests/: ../build/run-test262 -c test262.conf -a (or tests/test262.py,
#       which also fetches test262 and can split the run over processes)
#
#       ECMA Test 262 Runner for QuickJS
#
#       Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Fabrice Bellard
#       Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Charlie Gordon
#
#       Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this
#       software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal in the Software
#       without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify,
#       merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to
#       permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following
#       conditions: the above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included
#       in all copies or substantial portions of the Software. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS
#       IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.
#
#==============================================================================================

